WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.309 --> 00:00:02.892
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.283
- I am married with a child,
but my husband cheated on me.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:19.603
Should I leave him?

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.663
Yes or no?

00:00:23.187 --> 00:00:25.859
(light music)

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.653
- [Narrator] We brought
together a group of strangers

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.071
to help an anonymous person

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.143
make one of their toughest decisions.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.618
- I went through his Apple Watch.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:39.740
I scroll up and it's the
whole sexual conversation.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.093
That was him being selfish,
so why not choose me?

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.048
- [Narrator] After hearing
the group's advice,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.634
which choice will this person make?

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.587
This is "The Dilemma".

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:11.863
- When I first heard the
dilemma, I stood on the no side

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.523
because I believe in second chances.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.538
- I knew that there was more information,

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:24.153
but my gut instinct was
like, it's a yes for now.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.170
- How long have you two been together?

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.297
- Six and a half years.

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.049
So we're a military couple,
so it was one of those,

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.428
I meet you, we fall in love, get married.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.389
What made us really close
was that we realized

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.765
we were from similar backgrounds.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:39.975
We both grew up in the Caribbean,

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.476
we both kind of liked the same music,

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:42.978
the same type of things.

00:01:43.109 --> 00:01:44.980
- Did he honestly admit that to you

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.649
or did you come about finding that out?

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:51.361
- I had three dreams that he cheated

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.489
and I was like, okay, I
need to check something.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.117
So I went in his Apple Watch and I saw it.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.245
The female was labeled
under a male's name,

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:01.622
and when I asked him about it, I said,

00:02:01.747 --> 00:02:03.749
"Hey, I just wanna figure this out."

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:05.751
He came clean right off the bat.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.961
He was out of the house before he cheated.

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:09.254
The reason why that happened

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.673
is because we got into a bit of a tussle.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:15.385
I came downstairs and he was
on the phone with said girl

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:16.970
because they worked together.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.430
There was a little rumor

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:21.433
that she liked to sleep with married men.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.811
We got in a tussle, he
was out of the house,

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.563
then he cheated.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.151
He pretty much went on a week-long binge

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.612
of going over to her house and drinking

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.322
and getting physical.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.449
- Was this just sex,

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.577
or was this a full-on affair relationship?

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.538
- He said for him, it was just sex.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.665
There wasn't any going out to dinner

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:49.336
or any crazy "I love you"
texts or "I miss you"

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.296
or anything like that.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.131
- Has it been a pattern?

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.134
And I would include
anything like pornography

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:57.511
or anything in that.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:58.345
- [Tiffany] With him?

00:02:58.463 --> 00:02:59.429
- [Alicia] Yes.

00:02:59.559 --> 00:03:02.516
- No, that was the first and
only time that I know of.

00:03:02.635 --> 00:03:04.893
- You said you have a son, right?

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.853
How has he been impacted by this?

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:07.688
Does he know?

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.148
- So he's four, so in the beginning,

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.361
because there was a time where
he wasn't living in the house

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:18.782
and my son would actually
cry at night, "I want daddy",

00:03:18.927 --> 00:03:22.773
and I was just like, it made me sad.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:30.877
- Is he doing anything or
has he suggested anything

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:32.754
to repair your relationship?

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.798
- So he wants to do marriage counseling,

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.051
but he wants to do individual
counseling for himself first,

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.761
which he's actually doing right now.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:43.293
And he tries to plan little
dates and stuff like that.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.053
He's trying, I guess.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.604
- [Director] So please move now

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:53.523
if you feel like you should
be standing on another side.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.407
Was there anything there that you're like,

00:04:00.547 --> 00:04:03.493
"Oh, maybe I should be on the other side?"

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:06.955
- I think one of them was,
he's going to therapy,

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:07.956
and at that point, I'm like,

00:04:08.077 --> 00:04:09.833
"Well, I mean, if he's doing the work

00:04:09.967 --> 00:04:12.919
"and you kinda sound like
that's something you want,

00:04:13.057 --> 00:04:16.347
"then maybe I'm on the wrong side."

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:22.970
- [Alicia] When your husband
was away, how did you feel?

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.790
- Being honest, I missed him a lot.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:31.688
I had to put up a wall to
where it was just like,

00:04:31.807 --> 00:04:33.273
"Don't feel anything."

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:36.776
I still have that question
in the back of my mind,

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:38.403
is it worth working out

00:04:38.542 --> 00:04:42.908
after he finishes his
therapy and everything?

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.633
- Do you feel like you'll
be happier without him?

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:50.665
- I feel like I could
probably hit the pinnacles

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.167
that I haven't hit yet.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.877
I think I'm that girl, you know?

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.922
And I think sometimes,
when you're with someone,

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.383
you don't have enough freedom
to go do certain things.

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:03.178
How it is right now, we're
still in the same living space.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:06.723
Call me a dumb (silence) but
yes, sometimes we have sex.

00:05:06.869 --> 00:05:08.813
Sometimes I have sex with other people.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.812
- If the trust is gone on your side,

00:05:12.937 --> 00:05:14.231
is your faith the only thing

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.983
that's kinda really tying
you to this marriage?

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.568
- Yes, that's a part of it.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:21.196
My son is a very minute part of it

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:22.739
because I don't want to
be one of those people

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.659
that stays because of the child.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:26.660
And then also,

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:30.914
the fact that he's taken all
the right steps for himself.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:34.292
He's finally admitting
his childhood trauma

00:05:34.429 --> 00:05:37.587
and just the stress of the job

00:05:37.731 --> 00:05:40.257
that he had around the
time that he was cheating.

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:43.969
I believe in people getting second chances

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.805
if they're deserving and
if they put in the work.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.098
- [Director] If your mind has changed

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.933
and you want to move to the other side,

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:52.060
this will be another
moment and opportunity

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.913
that you can do that.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:08.243
- I stayed where I was, hesitantly.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:12.122
I kept coming back to the fact

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:15.083
that her husband was making an effort.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:18.336
I think love is work,
love is a lot of work.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.255
- I wanted to go to the no side.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.673
I wanted it to work.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:25.343
They've talked about it before,
he's working on himself,

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:29.139
but I just felt in my
heart and in my bones,

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:32.100
I was like, I think they're
better off just separate.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:33.310
- Air Force.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.228
Ex-husband, Air Force.

00:06:35.359 --> 00:06:36.062
- You get it!

00:06:36.192 --> 00:06:37.564
- Met in tech school.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:39.858
I got stationed here in LA.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:43.862
I deployed to Detroit to help
with the vaccines out there,

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:47.198
came back and found out
he was cheating on me

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.410
with one of the closest
people that I had met

00:06:50.528 --> 00:06:52.203
back in our old base.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.124
Going through the divorce,
it (silence) broke me down,

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:59.252
but I am finally getting to live a life

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:01.004
that I'm actually proud of.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:03.214
- If he's doing the work and
the reciprocation is there

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.217
and he wants to, then it
would change my answer.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:10.180
But then, if there's still no trust,

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.015
then that's where my struggle is.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:13.850
- In her situation, it
sounds like her husband

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:15.852
is taking those initial steps,

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:18.104
the very beginning steps, to do that.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.814
- I think it comes down to trust.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:20.940
At the end of the day,

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.043
do you think he's gonna do this again?

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.250
- Do you still trust him?

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:27.197
- (silence) no.

00:07:27.316 --> 00:07:29.741
(group laughs)

00:07:29.852 --> 00:07:32.535
I can do better, but then
you have all those factors

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:36.539
like our son and stuff
that we built together, so.

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:38.792
- My parents got divorced
when I was really little

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:41.252
and when you're a kid, you start to think,

00:07:41.377 --> 00:07:45.507
"I wish they were still
together", but now knowing more,

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:48.718
if they were together, my life
would've been a lot worse.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:50.720
I mean, it sucks to have
parents that are divorced

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:52.931
or that fight or anything like that,

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:57.477
but sometimes it's not
worth fighting for as much.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:59.000
- If I was your best friend,

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.023
I would say divorce is still on the table

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:03.670
but you're angry right now

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:09.030
and you need to work through that anger.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:12.033
I think it would be good
if he is a part of that

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:16.953
and gets to understand
what he has done to you.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:20.417
- I was with a man for 10 years,

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:23.169
spent all of my 20s with
him, had a baby by him,

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:25.630
gave him everything, and he cheated.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.215
I stayed.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:30.468
He had great days of being amazing,

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:33.471
but there was always that fear as well of,

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.763
what happens when you're not enough again?

00:08:37.457 --> 00:08:40.124
(pensive music)

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:53.241
- [Vidalia] Personally I feel
like they would be better off

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:54.492
handling their own situations.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.452
- [Kekona] Exactly.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:56.286
- [All] Separately.

00:08:56.423 --> 00:08:57.120
- [Justin K] Exactly.

00:08:57.256 --> 00:08:58.455
- [Kekona] If she's still genuinely feels

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:01.166
like she could be happier on the outside,

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:02.083
then I would say go for it.

00:09:02.223 --> 00:09:04.461
- [Vidalia] She should do it.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:06.046
- [Alicia] Things happened so fast

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:09.132
and they desperately need...

00:09:09.269 --> 00:09:10.633
- [Both] To slow down.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:11.468
- [Justin J] Divorce is final.

00:09:11.603 --> 00:09:13.136
- [Alicia] Yeah.

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:16.055
- [Justin J] It's hard to
repair the trust that was lost,

00:09:16.175 --> 00:09:18.008
but I believe you can.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:29.235
- For me, the most
important is to remember you

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:32.322
and not letting any of the outside noise,

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:35.825
meaning your friends, your
family, the naysayers,

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:39.412
dare I say religion, keep you in that box

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:42.040
if you decide that you
are no longer happy.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:45.043
- Maybe this relationship is salvageable.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:49.881
Things that break can come
back better than ever,

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:51.424
can come back stronger than ever,

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.193
if they're given that chance.

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:57.138
But divorce is still an option,

00:09:57.281 --> 00:09:59.613
even if you choose to stay for now.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.393
- [Director] Tiffany, can
you just kind of tell us

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:04.023
how you're feeling right now?

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:10.109
- Still a bit confused,

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:15.033
however I feel like I have a decision.

00:10:15.877 --> 00:10:18.377
(light music)

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:31.577
That's my man and I'm
gonna stick beside him

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:37.253
in another lifetime, okay.

00:10:43.052 --> 00:10:45.562
(light music)

00:10:45.694 --> 00:10:48.982
This weekend actually, I
ordered some moving boxes,

00:10:49.091 --> 00:10:51.985
so I guess I'm gonna start packing.

00:10:52.129 --> 00:10:55.655
I am gonna drive cross
country, hopefully with a buddy

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.324
and I'm gonna live with
my dad for a while.

00:10:58.449 --> 00:10:59.826
In this situation, it's not just me.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.953
It's me and it's my son.

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.038
I just wanna get out of the space,

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:07.563
and I think with time, the
actual paperwork will come.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:12.964
But as far as me in the
physical and me in the mental,

00:11:13.075 --> 00:11:15.800
I pretty much think I'm divorced.

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:18.261
To whoever is watching this,

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:21.843
go where you're celebrated,
not where you're tolerated.

00:11:23.316 --> 00:11:25.816
(group claps)

00:11:28.424 --> 00:11:31.091
(group talking)

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:42.560
Honestly, the best advice,
the best support sometimes

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:44.373
comes from strangers.

